{"id":"362bc2b8-ca4b-4209-b1c7-74593c534fe8","object":"chat.completion","created":1793257789,"model":"deepseek-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"\n\n<｜｜DSML｜｜ calls>\n<｜｜DSML｜｜ invoke name=\"read_range\">\n<｜｜DSML｜｜ parameter name=\"path\" string=\"true\">deepinfer/environ.py</｜｜DSML｜｜ parameter>\n<｜｜DSML｜｜ parameter name=\"start_line\" string=\"false\">95</｜｜DSML｜｜ parameter>\n<｜｜DSML｜｜ parameter name=\"end_line\" string=\"false\">230</｜｜DSML｜｜ parameter>\n</｜｜DSML｜｜ invoke>\n<｜｜DSML｜｜ invoke name=\"read_range\">\n<｜｜DSML｜｜ parameter name=\"path\" string=\"true\">deepinfer/logger.py</｜｜DSML｜｜ parameter>\n<｜｜DSML｜｜ parameter name=\"start_line\" string=\"false\">1</｜｜DSML｜｜ parameter>\n<｜｜DSML｜｜ parameter name=\"end_line\" string=\"false\">32</｜｜DSML｜｜ parameter>\n</｜｜DSML｜｜ invoke>\n<｜｜DSML｜｜ invoke name=\"read_range\">\n<｜｜DSML｜｜ parameter name=\"path\" string=\"true\">deepinfer/logger.py</｜｜DSML｜｜ parameter>\n<｜｜DSML｜｜ parameter name=\"start_line\" string=\"false\">107</｜｜DSML｜｜ parameter>\n<｜｜DSML｜｜ parameter name=\"end_line\" string=\"false\">140</｜｜DSML｜｜ parameter>\n</｜｜DSML｜｜ invoke>\n</｜｜DSML｜｜ calls>","reasoning_content":"Let me check current state. I need to see the files' content fully. Let me get the current status and relevant sections of the files.\n\nI have read_file results for all three files (hashes given). But my context doesn't have full content. I have key mechanisms. Let me read the specific regions I need: environ.py end (descriptors definitions), logger.py top imports and end, stats_logger worker function (already have lines 116-126).\n\nLet me plan the edits:\n\n1. environ.py: add to `envs` class attribute `log_max_message_chars: int | None = EnvVar.int_or_none_something`. Need >=32 validation with var name in error. Note EnvVar.__get__ wraps exception with f\"{self.name}: {e}\" so error text contains variable name automatically. Good — so I just need a factory that parses None -> None, else int and check >=32.\n\nAdd a static factory method `int_or_none_min(*, minimum: int)`. Let me add:\n\n```python\n    @staticmethod\n    def int_or_none_min(*, minimum: int) -> EnvVar[int | None]:\n        def _init(v: str | None) -> int | None:\n            if v is None:\n                return None\n            try:\n                value = int(v)\n            except ValueError:\n                raise ValueError(f\"{v!r} is not a valid integer\") from None\n            if value < minimum:\n                raise ValueError(f\"{value} must be >= {minimum}\")\n            return value\n        return EnvVar(_init)\n```\nEmpty string: int(\"\") raises ValueError -> wrapped with name. Good. Note `int` may accept whitespace and \"+64\", that's Python int parse; fine.\n\nThen in envs class: `log_max_message_chars: int | None = EnvVar.int_or_none_min(minimum=32)`.\n\nNeed to see the envs class body to find a spot. Let me read environ.py lines ~95-230.\n\n2. logger.py: formatter with max_message_chars keyword-only, and _setup_logger passes it from envs config.\n\nImplementation: in format(), after computing record.message etc. Need to truncate message body only, not prefix. Approach: compute the final message string via super().format(record), then... Truncation must happen before format actually. Better: create a copy of record with truncated msg? Spec says must not mutate shared record's msg/args/exc_info/stack_info. We can build text manually: but spec says keep prefixes.\n\nSimplest: in format, create shallow copy record via `logging.makeLogRecord(record.__dict__)`? That copies. Hmm, but exception formatting: super().format uses record.exc_info and appends traceback to output — that's fine, we want traceback intact. If we copy the record, exc_info preserved.\n\nPlan:\n```python\ndef format(self, record):\n    max_chars = self.max_message_chars\n    if max_chars is not None and getattr(record, \"keep_full_message\", None) is not True:\n        # compute message after args substitution